From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:35:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: Read the Wake on LAN override from an
 option

PchPmWolEnableOverride makes FSP-S set WOL_EN_OVRD in GEN_PMCON_B: the
PCH then takes the wake of its LAN from S4 and S5 whatever PME_EN says.
The ACPI tables of the SoC give the GbE device wakes up to S4
(pch_glan.asl, _PRW with 4), so an OS that honours them, as Linux does,
does not arm it for S5, and without the override a computer that was
shut down does not wake on LAN. The reference code of Intel has it as
the "Wake on LAN Enable" setup option, on by default.

Read the "wake_on_lan" option, with the devicetree setting as its
default, so that the boards that do not offer it keep what they set.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x, which offers it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c
index 8aed7b2c2c..bd2e808c33 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/fsp_params.c
@@ -436,9 +436,9 @@ void platform_fsp_silicon_init_params_cb(FSPS_UPD *supd)
 	s_cfg->DdiPortDDdc = config->DdiPortDDdc;
 	s_cfg->DdiPortFDdc = config->DdiPortFDdc;
 
-	/* WOL */
+	/* WOL: the override, from S4 and S5, is the "wake_on_lan" option */
 	s_cfg->PchPmPcieWakeFromDeepSx = config->LanWakeFromDeepSx;
-	s_cfg->PchPmWolEnableOverride = config->WolEnableOverride;
+	s_cfg->PchPmWolEnableOverride = get_uint_option("wake_on_lan", config->WolEnableOverride);
 
 	/* disable Legacy PME */
 	memset(s_cfg->PcieRpPmSci, 0, sizeof(s_cfg->PcieRpPmSci));
